            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to faint, then the Bengali for bedridden."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ওষুধ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ওষুধ — oshudh — \"a medicine; medicine\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সকালে আর রাতে এই ওষুধটা খেতে হবে। sôkāle ār rāte ei oshudhṭā khete hôbe. This medicine has to be taken morning and night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Bengali eats its medicine: ওষুধ (oshudh) খাওয়া, to take medicine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ওষুধ (oshudh) comes from Sanskrit auṣadha, \"consisting of herbs\", and so \"herbs, a remedy\" (CDIAL 2571), worn down in Bengali speech."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
