          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সেরে ওঠা — sere oṭhā — \"to recover; to get well\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দুই সপ্তাহ পরে অরুণ জ্বর থেকে সেরে উঠল। dui sôptāhô pôre ôrun jbôr theke sere uṭhlô. Two weeks later Arun recovered from the fever."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি শিগগির সেরে উঠলেন, tini shiggir sere uṭhlen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সেরে ওঠা (sere oṭhā) is sere, the -এ form of sārā, \"to get well\", the plain partner of সারানো (taught), to repair, with oṭhā, \"to rise\" (CDIAL 1793)."
            }
          ]
        },
